ction titled, “Yarrow’s Business—Yarrow’s License Agreement—GenSci License Agreement” included in our definitive proxy statement/prospectus filed on Form S-4 with the SEC, most recently amended on June 3, 2026, declared effective on June 15, 2026.","context":"GenSci License Agreement","section":"Business and Macroeconomic Conditions","block":355,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosure","interpretation":"source_excerpt_not_independently_verified","source":{"accession":"0001566044-26-000010","form":"10-Q","filedAt":"2026-08-13","reportDate":"2026-06-30","cik":"0001566044","url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/1566044/000156604426000010/vyne-20260630.htm","rawPath":"sec/raw/f6491d728dfd88c32f8541482df4436fe17ee5dbc818b385687651e5036e1ff6.bin","sha256":"f6491d728dfd88c32f8541482df4436fe17ee5dbc818b385687651e5036e1ff6"}},{"id":"03ae2ebc7025fafa6a148bdb5b4f05c879d35eca99059b83c26a6b7f5a72c2d2","quote":"Historically, the legacy VYNE business generated revenues under development and license agreements, including royalty payments from sales of Finacea foam. We previously licensed the rights to Finacea to LEO Pharma A/S (\"LEO Pharma\"). Formulation and use patents for Finacea foam currently expire in 2027 and 2029, respectively, but may experience an earlier loss of exclusivity due to generic entry. On June 11, 2026, LEO Pharma notified us of its decision to terminate the Finacea license agreement effective December 31, 2026. As a result, we do not expect to recognize Finacea royalty revenue for periods after December 31, 2026. For both the three months ended June 30, 2026 and 2025, royalty revenues from LEO Pharma in connection with sales of Finacea were $0.1 million. For the six months ended June 30, 2026 and 2025, royalty revenues from LEO Pharma in connection with sales of Finacea were $0.2 million and $0.3 million, respectively.","context":"Revenues","section":"Business and Macroeconomic Conditions","block":358,"table":null,"attribution":"issuer_disclosur